From abc2546b9d8ee0688638988e8e4b45064f3e57da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cyril Rohr <hey@cyrilrohr.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:16:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] remotecache/gha: honor compression attributes

The gha cache exporter returned a hardcoded compression.New(compression.
Default) from Config(), so compression, compression-level and
force-compression passed to --export-cache type=gha were silently ignored
and every layer was exported as gzip, as the s3 exporter did before the
previous commit.

Finalize already records each layer's media type in the cache config and
the importer reads it back, so blobs of any supported compression
round-trip. Like the s3 backend, parse the attributes when resolving the
exporter and return them from Config(). The importer shares getConfig and
keeps ignoring them. NewExporter keeps the default compression.

The test builds a runtime token with golang-jwt, which becomes a direct
dependency in go.mod.

Signed-off-by: Cyril Rohr <hey@cyrilrohr.com>
